	quest.7DE996D5FD88B1F3.quest_desc: [
		"Unless you've found a way to generate lava, it can get very annoying to keep having to refill the lava tank. "
		""
		"Replace the floor with &epowered heating coils&r and replace the fluid tank with a &ecapacitor&r, and the foundry will run on electricity! You then only need to supply power to the capacitor for it to run."
	]
	quest.7DE996D5FD88B1F3.title: "Electric Upgrade"
	quest.7DF3981485FECDEA.quest_desc: [
		"So, now you have a cooking table! You also got &#FFC3F012 basic kitchen floors&r and a &#FFC3F0kitchen counter&r as a reward."
		""
		"If you use the kitchen floor as, well, flooring, any Cooking for Blockhead items you place on the floor will &dautomatically connect&r. Put down the kitchen floor, then the cooking table and counter on top, right next to each other."
		""
		"Store your ingredients and Pam's cookware in the kitchen counter. Interact with the cooking table - if you have enough ingredients to make a recipe, &dit should automatically show up!&r"
	]
	quest.7EEAFAA528DD378A.quest_desc: ["This massive multiblock machine can smelt up to 12 items at a time, it is also very load and WILL scare your neighbours."]
	quest.7EEAFAA528DD378A.title: "Arc Furnace"
	quest.7F2020DF1793E40E.quest_desc: ["The Crude Blast Furnace is your first way to create &eSteel&r. Steel has a wide variety of uses and also unlocks building Oritech machines."]
	quest.7F2020DF1793E40E.title: "Crude Blast Furnace"
	quest.7F785C3031832DCE.quest_desc: [
		"&dGardens&r are one of the main ways to get ingredients which you can &#FFC3F0plant&r. They spawn in the overworld, and usually look a bit like shrubs."
		""
		"&dGardens&r are biome specific, so you may have to explore to find different varieties. Some ingredients only drop from certain gardens - &#DAFFB5spinach&r only drops from &dfrost gardens&r, and &#DAFFB5tomatoes&r only drop from &dshaded gardens&r."
	]
	quest.7F785C3031832DCE.title: "Gardens"
